TASK: Redesign and complete the BlueMind Search experience.

GOAL:
Build a premium BlueMind Universal Search experience.

IMPORTANT:
Do NOT copy ChatGPT visually.
Use the search UX principles only:
- organized categories
- useful results
- compact search while typing
- clear result types
- easy navigation

The final design must clearly look like BlueMind:
- black background
- BlueMind green identity where appropriate
- existing Apple/iOS glass components
- existing native glass circular buttons
- BlueMind spacing, typography and interaction style

==================================================
1. SEARCH HEADER
==================================================

The Search screen should have a clean iOS header.

Top area:
- circular glass Back button on the left
- centered title: “Search”
- circular glass X button on the right

BACK:
- returns to the previous screen/state
- does NOT reset unrelated navigation

X:
- completely exits Search
- closes keyboard
- clears temporary search UI state
- returns to the screen from which Search was opened

Back and X must have different behavior.

Use the existing BlueMind native Apple-glass buttons.
Do not create fake CSS circles if reusable native glass controls already exist.

==================================================
2. UNIVERSAL SEARCH CATEGORIES
==================================================

Search should NOT be limited to conversations.

Add horizontally scrollable filters:

All
Chats
Images
Documents
Projects

Potential future categories can be added later without redesigning the screen.

Default:
All

Selected tab:
- clear BlueMind glass selected state
- subtle animation
- do not use oversized solid pills

Unselected tabs:
- minimal and readable

When selecting a category, update results immediately.

==================================================
3. SEARCH FIELD
==================================================

Search field placeholder:

“Search BlueMind…”

Use a premium Apple-glass search field.

Include:
- search icon
- typed text
- clear X button when text exists

Behavior:
- tapping field opens iOS keyboard
- search updates while typing
- use sensible debounce to avoid excessive backend requests
- clearing text returns to initial/recent state
- preserve Unicode correctly

Search must work properly with:
- English
- Arabic
- Swedish
- numbers
- emojis
- mixed-language queries

Do NOT break RTL Arabic text.

Do NOT display URL-encoded filenames such as:
%C3%A4
%20
etc.

Decode filenames before displaying them.

==================================================
4. KEYBOARD / ACTIVE SEARCH MODE
==================================================

When the keyboard is CLOSED:
Keep the normal BlueMind Search layout.

When the user starts typing and keyboard OPENS:
transition into a compact search mode.

The results should receive maximum usable vertical space.

The search field may move into a compact floating position immediately above the keyboard.

If implemented:
- animate the transition smoothly
- keep correct iOS safe-area spacing
- never overlap the keyboard
- never overlap results
- never duplicate the search field

IMPORTANT:
This is Search mode, NOT Chat mode.

While Search is active NEVER show:
- Ask anything composer
- chat attachment +
- microphone from chat composer
- send button
- chat navigation toolbar

Only the Search field belongs above the keyboard.

==================================================
5. SEARCH RESULTS
==================================================

Results should be clean and information-dense.

Every result should contain:

LEFT:
Type-specific icon/thumbnail.

CENTER:
Title
+
one short contextual preview/snippet.

OPTIONAL:
small metadata when useful.

Examples:

CHAT
[chat icon]
“AI Plan Design”
“...we changed the plan builder to…”

DOCUMENT
[document icon]
“CV_Rokaia_Ghaith_4.docx”
Document

IMAGE
[thumbnail/icon]
“BlueMind UI Concept”
Image

PROJECT
[project icon]
“University App”
Project • updated recently

Do not show unnecessary technical information.

==================================================
6. RESULT TYPE ICONS
==================================================

Use a consistent BlueMind icon system:

Chats:
conversation bubble

Images:
real thumbnail when available;
otherwise image icon

Documents:
document/file icon appropriate to type

Projects:
project/folder icon

Icons should use BlueMind's existing visual language.

Do not use emojis as UI icons.

==================================================
7. RESULT ORDERING
==================================================

For “All”, rank results intelligently.

Priority should consider:
1. exact title match
2. strong title match
3. content match
4. recent relevant items
5. weaker matches

Do NOT simply dump database order.

Searching:
“Python”

should prioritize:
“Python Study Plan”
before an unrelated conversation that happens to contain “Python” once.

==================================================
8. SEARCH MATCH HIGHLIGHTING
==================================================

Highlight the matching part subtly.

Example:

Search:
Python

Result:
Learn [Python] Easily

Use a subtle BlueMind accent/glass treatment.

Do not use aggressive bright highlighting.

Support highlighting inside snippets where practical.

==================================================
9. CHAT RESULTS
==================================================

When a Chat result is tapped:
- open that exact conversation
- restore its messages
- exit Search correctly

Search result menus may use the existing native iOS three-dot menu if actions already exist.

Do not invent duplicate chat actions.

==================================================
10. IMAGE RESULTS
==================================================

When an Image result is tapped:
- open the correct existing BlueMind image viewer
- preserve the image reference/context

Use actual thumbnails where available.

Avoid large thumbnails that waste vertical space.

==================================================
11. DOCUMENT RESULTS
==================================================

Documents should display:
- decoded filename
- document type/icon
- useful metadata where available

Tap:
open the existing document/file viewer.

Do not expose internal storage paths.

==================================================
12. PROJECT RESULTS
==================================================

Projects must appear in Universal Search.

Display:
- project name
- optional short description
- useful small metadata

Tap:
open the exact Project by projectId.

Do NOT identify Projects by display name.

==================================================
13. EMPTY SEARCH STATE
==================================================

If no results exist:

Show a clean BlueMind empty state.

Example:

“No results found”

“Try another word or search another category.”

Do not leave a completely blank screen.

==================================================
14. INITIAL STATE
==================================================

Before the user types, show useful content.

Prefer:
- Recent Searches
and/or
- Recent items

Keep this lightweight.

Do NOT fabricate fake recent searches.

Only show real user data if available.

==================================================
15. LOADING STATE
==================================================

Do not flash old results while a new query is loading.

Use a subtle BlueMind loading state.

Avoid large spinners.

Search should feel immediate.

==================================================
16. SEARCH BACKEND
==================================================

Inspect the current backend before creating anything new.

Reuse existing search capabilities where possible.

Universal Search should support authenticated searching across:
- user's chats
- user's images
- user's documents/files
- user's projects

SECURITY:
Every result MUST belong to the authenticated user.

Never trust a userId supplied by the client.

Use server-side authenticated identity.

A user must NEVER be able to search another user's:
- chats
- files
- images
- projects

==================================================
17. SEARCH RESULT DATA MODEL
==================================================

Normalize results so the frontend receives a predictable structure.

Conceptually:

{
  id,
  type,
  title,
  snippet,
  thumbnail,
  metadata,
  updatedAt
}

Do not expose sensitive internal fields.

Use existing project architecture rather than creating unnecessary duplicate models.

==================================================
18. PERFORMANCE
==================================================

Search must remain fast with large histories.

Implement:
- debounce
- result limits/pagination where necessary
- efficient database queries
- appropriate indexes if required

Do not download the user's entire history to the iPhone and filter everything locally if server-side search is appropriate.

==================================================
19. IOS GLASS DESIGN
==================================================

Apply the existing BlueMind Apple/iOS glass system to INTERACTIVE controls:

- Back
- X
- Search field
- category filters
- clear-search control
- result menus
- any filter/action controls

Do not make every result card excessively blurry.

Content must remain easy to read.

Use glass to communicate interaction, not as decoration everywhere.

==================================================
20. MOTION
==================================================

Use subtle native-feeling transitions for:

- opening Search
- focusing Search
- keyboard appearing
- category switching
- clearing query
- opening results
- exiting Search

No excessive animations.

Respect the existing BlueMind Animations setting if applicable.

==================================================
21. SEARCH STATE
==================================================

Search state must behave correctly.

If user:
Searches -> opens result -> presses Back

return to Search with:
- previous query
- selected category
- scroll position where practical

If user presses X:
exit Search completely.

